							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=2209.msg28300#msg28300">Quote from: dj100proof on May 23, 2007, 11:42:26 am</a></div><div class="quote">I&#039;m just looking forward to the &#039;look at how far we&#039;ve come&#039; Beijing Olympics. What a joke. <br /></div><br />I could see both sides on this one. Yes, there are still an assload of problems, but a grip of them (mainly public corruption) are also in the process of being reformed. There was a huge dragnet launched in Shanghai recently that rooted out corrupt officials including city officers and even the mayor. Also, private corruption is also getting cracked down upon, especially regarding labor contracts, unequal debt settling and falsifiable contracting. There was even a program launched a while back (although only&nbsp; shortly successful) called <img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Smileys/default/huh.gif" alt="Huh" border="0" />? that aimed to improve economic conditions in the western regions. A lot of things are still fucked up though, but how do you manage the world&#039;s most populous country without problems?</div>
